F000482.text:
RT by @RepFedorchak: “The losses we are experiencing are staggering and unsustainable. Our farms and factories won’t be able to hold on much longer if the U.S. cannot control the artificially and destructively cheap foreign sugar imports that are undercutting American-made sugar,” says Brent Baldwin, a fourth-generation sugarbeet farmer from St. Thomas, North Dakota.

@SenJohnHoeven and @RepFedorchak, two of the members who led this week's letter to @USTradeRep, represent the largest sugarbeet producing region in the country and one of the most efficient sugarbeet production regions in the world. We are thankful to have champions like Senator Hoeven and Congresswoman Fedorchak who understand the importance of keeping sugar production in America.

Read our full press release here ➡️ https://bit.ly/3RmkgiM
